Orange custard tart
6
Custard tart flavoured with orange juice and zest, on puff pastry.

---
Pastry
puff pastry|1|sheet

Orange custard
orange juice|1|l
eggs|6|pcs
unwaxed orange|1|pcs
powdered sugar|150|g
wheat flour|60|g
custard powder|60|g
soft butter|30|g

---
Preheat the oven to 180°C.
Bring the orange juice to the boil.
In a bowl, mix the eggs and sugar.
Add the flour and custard powder, mix until smooth.
Pour the boiling orange juice into the mixture gradually while whisking.
Return to low heat and cook 2 to 3 min after it boils, stirring, until thick.
Add the finely grated orange zest and the butter, mix.

Butter a round tin.
Line the tin with the puff pastry.
Pour the orange custard into the pastry case.
Bake about 40 min at 180°C.
Let cool completely before turning out and serving.

---
You can flavour the custard with spices (cinnamon, star anise…) or replace some of the orange juice with chocolate or coffee pastry cream.
The tart turns out more easily when fully cold.

